WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.907
Welcome to Module 9.

00:00:01.907 --> 00:00:10.002
In this module, we are moving from regular Python collections into one of the most important tools for

00:00:10.002 --> 00:00:11.357
numerical analytics: NumPy.

00:00:11.357 --> 00:00:18.592
NumPy gives us arrays, which are designed for working efficiently with many numeric values at the same time.

00:00:18.592 --> 00:00:25.022
Instead of writing a loop for every small calculation, we can often describe the calculation once and let

00:00:25.022 --> 00:00:28.307
NumPy apply it across an entire array.

00:00:28.307 --> 00:00:31.507
Our goal is not to memorize every NumPy function.

00:00:31.507 --> 00:00:34.752
The goal is to become comfortable with array thinking.

00:00:34.752 --> 00:00:43.042
We will create arrays, inspect their structure, perform vectorized calculations, select values, reshape data,

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:49.222
work with rows and columns, generate random data, and summarize numeric results.

00:00:49.222 --> 00:00:55.167
These skills appear again in Pandas, statistics, visualization, machine learning, and scientific computing.

00:00:55.167 --> 00:01:02.232
So while NumPy may look like one library among many, the ideas you learn here will support much

00:01:02.232 --> 00:01:04.931
of the analytics work you do later.
